            <div xml:id="d249">

                <pb facs="0408" n="308" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg308"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.D1/138</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 939 Political</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-12">June 12, 1934</date>.<lb/>[Received June
                        22.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith two
                    communications from the Secretary-General of the High Commission for Refugees
                        <pb facs="0409" n="309" xml:id="pg309"/> coming from Germany, both dated
                    June 2, 1934 and addressed to the Secretary of State, which have just been
                    received in this office.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Prentiss B.
                    Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>




